1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:00,380
Oy!

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:02,800
Listen to that sound.

3
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:04,040
Oiii!

4
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,460
Two spellings make it.

5
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,780
Oi, and oy.

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,530
You hear it in coin.

7
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:13,760
And in toy.

8
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:17,120
Same sound, different spelling.

9
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:18,920
So which one do we write?

10
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:22,740
It's the same secret as always.

11
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,960
WHERE the sound sits.

12
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,620
Beginning, middle, or end.

13
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,560
In the MIDDLE of a word, we write oi.

14
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:33,260
C.

15
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:34,540
Oi.

16
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:35,440
N.

17
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:36,960
Coin!

18
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:40,780
Letters before it, letters after it.

19
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,490
At the END of a word, we write oy.

20
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:46,460
T.

21
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:47,540
Oy.

22
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:49,060
Toy!

23
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:51,220
Nothing follows it.

24
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:52,860
So it's oy.

25
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,640
We never write toi.

26
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,610
And we never write coyn.

27
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,170
Oi in the middle.

28
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:02,900
Oy at the end.

29
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:04,540
Let's see it.

30
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:06,440
Coin.

31
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,180
Soil.

32
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:09,860
Point.

33
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:11,860
Oil.

34
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,060
Join.

35
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:15,960
Boil.

36
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:19,060
All oi, all in the middle.

37
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:20,960
Now the end.

38
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:22,640
Boy.

39
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:24,600
Toy.

40
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:26,720
Joy.

41
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:28,460
Enjoy.

42
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:31,120
Annoy.

43
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:33,240
Coy.

44
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:36,200
All oy, all at the end.

45
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:38,220
Your turn!

46
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:39,540
Here's the word.

47
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,100
Enjoy.

48
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,100
Is it oi, or oy?

49
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,220
It's oy!

50
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:49,480
Because the sound is right at the end.

51
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,360
So remember.

52
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:55,300
Oi sits in the middle, oy jumps to the end.

53
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:59,640
Learn every spelling rule in the English Learning app.

54
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:01,720
Free, and made for kids!
